WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:18.277
19 Dear Daddy Longlegs, Here I am at Mrs.

2
00:00:18.357 --> 00:00:19.938
Paterson's cottage by the sea.

3
00:00:21.299 --> 00:00:24.241
My window looks out on the loveliest landscape.

4
00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:27.184
Or seascape, I guess.

5
00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:32.348
Water, rocks, and sky are all I can see.

6
00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:37.529
Did I describe my job in my last letter?

7
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.513
Mrs. Paterson's older daughter, Marion, is starting college this fall.

8
00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:46.516
I'm tutoring her in English, Latin, and algebra.

9
00:00:48.597 --> 00:00:52.020
I'm also working on English and Latin with Florence, the younger daughter.

10
00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:55.042
And what a job it is!

11
00:00:55.062 --> 00:01:00.326
I don't know how Marion is going to succeed at college.

12
00:01:01.607 --> 00:01:03.008
And Florence is hopeless!

13
00:01:04.584 --> 00:01:06.365
Pretty, but not very bright.

14
00:01:08.905 --> 00:01:10.366
On my first morning, Mrs.

15
00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:12.526
Paterson asked me to come into her study.

16
00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.947
"I know you're the girls' tutor," Mrs.

17
00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:16.727
Paterson said.

18
00:01:16.747 --> 00:01:20.308
"But I don't want you working them too hard."

19
00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:22.389
"No, ma'am."

20
00:01:23.769 --> 00:01:26.310
"I want them to spend most of the day outdoors.

21
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.071
Perhaps you can find a pretty place to set up your classroom."

22
00:01:32.772 --> 00:01:33.632
"I'll try, ma'am.

23
00:01:33.996 --> 00:01:37.358
But if Marion's going to start college, she'll need to concentrate."

24
00:01:37.378 --> 00:01:40.460
"I'm sure you'll figure out what to do."

25
00:01:42.061 --> 00:01:42.982
And with that Mrs.

26
00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:44.763
Paterson went back to reading a letter.

27
00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:51.628
So I took the girls outside, and we tramped around until we found a spot hidden in the

28
00:01:51.688 --> 00:01:57.352
cliffs. At first, even I had trouble concentrating.

29
00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:03.696
Every time a ship passed by, I thought of sailing to Europe.

30
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.641
And I wondered what I was missing.

31
00:02:06.661 --> 00:02:10.623
"I'll never understand any of this!"

32
00:02:12.024 --> 00:02:14.125
Marion tossed her math book onto the ground.

33
00:02:14.145 --> 00:02:19.008
"Mother is making me go to college, but I don't see why.

34
00:02:20.108 --> 00:02:21.589
It's a girls' college too.

35
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.111
How am I supposed to find a husband there?"

36
00:02:25.131 --> 00:02:30.915
"If you get an education, then you'll be able to work," I said.

37
00:02:33.692 --> 00:02:38.935
Florence giggled, and Marion said, "Married women don't have time to work!"

38
00:02:40.816 --> 00:02:41.696
I frowned at them.

39
00:02:41.716 --> 00:02:45.038
"Don't you want to learn math and grammar?"

40
00:02:45.058 --> 00:02:49.481
"I've got no use for math," Marion said.

41
00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.662
"And grammar is boring!"

42
00:02:52.682 --> 00:02:56.164
"I agree," Florence chimed in.

43
00:02:56.184 --> 00:03:00.427
"I worry about you two," I murmured.

44
00:03:01.927 --> 00:03:02.668
And it was true.

45
00:03:03.788 --> 00:03:05.989
Their conversation is so boring.

46
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.611
But I suppose that won't matter if they marry boring men.

47
00:03:11.972 --> 00:03:14.593
I've certainly met quite a few boring ones this summer!

48
00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.695
Fortunately, I only have to tutor the girls for half the day.

49
00:03:19.695 --> 00:03:22.136
By the way, I received a letter from Jervie.

50
00:03:23.397 --> 00:03:25.838
It's quite a short letter from Paris.

51
00:03:27.398 --> 00:03:31.120
He's still upset that I refused to follow his advice about going to Europe.

52
00:03:32.468 --> 00:03:36.471
He says if he gets back in time, he'll see me for a few days at Lock Willow

53
00:03:36.511 --> 00:03:39.613
Farm. (If he gets back in time!

54
00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:42.895
Does he expect me to sit around, hoping he'll arrive?)

55
00:03:44.396 --> 00:03:46.758
I think he'll forgive me for staying here this summer.

56
00:03:47.578 --> 00:03:50.520
But I'll probably have to be very sweet and docile.

57
00:03:52.381 --> 00:03:54.123
I also received a letter from Sallie.

58
00:03:55.343 --> 00:03:58.746
She wants me to come to their summer house for two weeks in September.

59
00:03:59.826 --> 00:04:01.888
Do I have to ask your permission to do that?

60
00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:05.409
Or am I old enough to do what I want?

61
00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:07.690
Never mind.

62
00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.491
I know I'm old enough because I'm a college senior.

63
00:04:11.872 --> 00:04:15.213
Having worked all summer, I feel like taking a vacation.

64
00:04:16.594 --> 00:04:18.435
I want to see the mountains and the lake.

65
00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:21.856
I want to see Sallie and her brother.

66
00:04:23.497 --> 00:04:25.218
Jimmy is going to teach me to canoe.

67
00:04:25.418 --> 00:04:26.118
That'll be fun!

68
00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:32.936
But here's my real motive for going to Sallie's.

69
00:04:32.956 --> 00:04:36.558
I want Jervie to arrive at Lock Willow and find that I'm not there.

70
00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.120
I know that's mean.

71
00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:45.063
But I MUST show him that he can't tell me what to do.

72
00:04:46.544 --> 00:04:50.406
The only person who can do that is you—and not all the time.

73
00:04:51.687 --> 00:04:52.527
I'm off to the woods!

74
00:04:53.968 --> 00:05:03.302
Yours ever, Judy September 6 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I'm at Sallie's summer house in the mountains.

75
00:05:04.643 --> 00:05:07.185
I'm pleased to say that I've been here for five days.

76
00:05:09.527 --> 00:05:11.348
By the time your letter arrived at Mrs.

77
00:05:11.408 --> 00:05:13.550
Paterson's cottage, I had already left.

78
00:05:15.652 --> 00:05:17.854
So I couldn't go to Lock Willow as you ordered.

79
00:05:19.055 --> 00:05:21.337
Mrs. Paterson forwarded your letter to me here.

80
00:05:22.317 --> 00:05:26.201
If you want me to obey in the future, tell your secretary to write more quickly.

81
00:05:27.622 --> 00:05:29.944
The woods are lovely, and so is the house.

82
00:05:32.096 --> 00:05:35.959
The weather is delightful, and I enjoy spending time with the McBrides.

83
00:05:37.941 --> 00:05:39.603
The whole world is wonderful.

84
00:05:40.063 --> 00:05:41.104
I'm very happy!

85
00:05:44.227 --> 00:05:45.468
Oh, I have to stop writing.

86
00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:48.490
Jimmy is calling me to go canoeing.

87
00:05:49.911 --> 00:05:54.375
Good-bye! Yours, Judy P.S.

88
00:05:54.896 --> 00:05:56.437
I'm sorry to have disobeyed you.

89
00:05:57.738 --> 00:05:59.580
But I'm curious about one thing.

90
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.043
Why are you so against my having a little fun?

91
00:06:04.965 --> 00:06:08.588
I worked hard all summer tutoring those ridiculous girls.

92
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.011
I deserve a break.

93
00:06:12.332 --> 00:06:15.396
In spite of all your faults, I still appreciate you.
